00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:52.040
So here are my top 5 favorite items from the
franchise and some of the lore behind them.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.890
Number 5 - The Goddess's Harp

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:57.880
In the timeline of the franchise the first
time Link gets this is in Skyward Sword as

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:02.420
a child, but it's also used by Princess Zelda
in Ocarina of Time and you could argue that

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:06.390
it's almost the same thing as the Harp of
Ages in the Oracle series on Gameboy Color.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.190
In Skyward Sword it functions a lot like the
Ocarina of Time in that it helps you unlock

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:14.250
new challenges in the game. But in the actual
Ocarina of Time game Zelda only uses the Goddess

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:18.230
Harp to teach you new Ocarina songs. So in
each game the same items get used in different

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.800
ways even though the lore is similar.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.560
As the name implies the Harp comes from the
goddess Hylia she was the goddess who stayed

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.840
behind to guard the triforce when the old
gods left Hyrule. She eventually chose to

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.120
take mortal form and became the progenitor
for the Hyrulian Royal family.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.440
In the franchise she became the first incarnation
of Zelda in skyward sword, but for example

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.540
in Ocarina of Time the Zelda we meet is her
descendant. In all of the games the royal

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:45.379
family descends from the goddess' bloodline
though.

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:48.489
The first time we actually met the gods was
in Ocarina of Time, but subsequent games continued

00:02:48.489 --> 00:02:49.680
to feature them.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.480
Number 4 - The Silver Arrow

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.370
Next to the master sword this is one of the
most important items in the franchise. In

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:59.330
the original NES games you use it to kill
Ganon at the end, and in later games in the

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:04.370
franchise they turned it into Light Arrows.
But they serve the same function. They also

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:07.170
cause enemies to drop hella extra rupees.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:10.730
In Twilight Princess you don't actually get
to use them, but Zelda does and they serve

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.239
the same function.

00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:16.640
In the lore they're generally just magical
arrows that literally pierce evil. In some

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:20.970
of the later games you find them in dungeons.
But in Ocarina of time Zelda keeps them in

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:24.250
the sacred realm until you wake all of the
sages.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:28.780
After Ocarina the sages were incorporated
into all aspects of the franchise. They serve

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:33.049
as the bridge between the sacred realm where
the triforce is kept and the physical world

00:03:33.049 --> 00:03:34.549
of Hyrule.

00:03:34.549 --> 00:03:36.310
Number 3 - The Magic Mirror

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:40.319
This only appears in Link to the Past and
you use it to travel between the light and

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:45.500
dark worlds but you can also use it as a warp
device inside dungeons. You obtain it by helping

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.970
the Lost Old Man. That's the only name he's
given, but in the lore he's a descendant of

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.840
the sages and you eventually have to rescue
his daughter who's one of the seven maidens.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:56.409
They're a group that appears in both Link
to the Past and the Four Swords games. In

00:03:56.409 --> 00:03:58.989
each of the installments you have to rescue
them.

00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:02.769
You also learn about the power of the mirror
from Sahasrahla who's also a descendant of

00:04:02.769 --> 00:04:09.769
the sages and helps teach you things 
in the game.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.920
Number 2 - The Hylian Shield

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:19.769
In the game it's the most powerful shield
you can get and also protects you from fire.

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:24.860
Usually the shield is purchased but Skyward
Sword introduced some more creative Lore.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:28.610
It's guarded by the dragon Lanayru who's one
of three sacred guardians appointed by the

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:30.900
goddess to watch over parts of Hyrule.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:35.620
The shield itself is most famous for it's
appearance. All incarnations of the franchise

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:40.639
have used the same based symbols which incorporate
aspects of the Goddess Crest, The Royal Crest

00:04:40.639 --> 00:04:45.669
and the Hylian Crest. It bears the Triforce
and the Crimson Loftwing. It's always been

00:04:45.669 --> 00:04:49.910
on the shield, but just like the dragon Skyward
Sword also turned the loftwing into an actual

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:56.910
bird you get bonded to like Daenerys is bonded
to her dragons on game of thrones.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:00.139
and my number 1 favorite item of Course - The
Master Sword

00:05:00.139 --> 00:05:04.530
I think my favorite animation in the series
is still Link yanking the master sword out

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:08.870
in the temple of time during Ocarina. The
sword was originally forged by the goddess

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:14.039
as the goddess sword and then is later reforged
into the master sword by Link.

00:05:14.039 --> 00:05:21.039
It's imbued with the spirit of Fi who is a
humanoid spirit representation of the goddess

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:25.580
and gives you tips that help you complete
your quests.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:30.860
Skyward Sword really takes the lore a lot
further and incorporates a dark version of

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:34.880
the sword weilded by Demise. But it's implied
that the goddess and the sages forged the

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.539
Goddess and Master Swords as a result of Demise
creating his version of the sword.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:42.949
It's a very chicken or the egg type argument
that gets even more complicated when the game

00:05:42.949 --> 00:05:44.880
incorporates time travel.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.860
Even though I've always thought of the Hero's
Bow and Light Arrows as the most important

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:53.780
weapon in the franchise, the Master Sword
is still the most identifiable in game item.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:55.949
Probably because of arthurian mythology and
excalibur.

